{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB00958 - MONDO_8170",
  "verbalization": "Carboplatin, a platinum-based chemotherapy agent, is implicated in the pathogenesis of ovarian cancer through a series of interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that Carboplatin is associated with Ovarian Cancer via the induration of Tretamine, a compound that acts as a mediator in the development of ovarian cancer. This relationship is supported by the fact that Carboplatin is linked to both Ovarian Endometrioid Adenocarcinoma and Malignant Sex Cord Stromal Tumor Of Ovary, which in turn are associated with Tretamine and ultimately Ovarian Cancer. The shared involvement of Tretamine across these pathways indicates a potential mechanism by which Carboplatin may contribute to the development of ovarian cancer, possibly through the activation of downstream signaling pathways that are also involved in the progression of other ovarian tumors. The consistent presence of Tretamine as a common mediator across different subtypes of ovarian cancer underscores the importance of this compound in the pathophysiology of the disease.",
